{"kind":"propose","text":"Exclude trust and reputation scoring from gitseq scope, explicitly and permanently: no gitseq deliverable - kernel, profile, projector, or shipped projection - computes actor reliability, promise-keeping scores, or any reputation valuation, and no gitseq-shipped authority check ever consumes one; roles stay granted and ratified, never computed. The record remains open and anyone may build such a projection outside the project - the exclusion is of our scope, not of their capability, and it is load-bearing that the durable log holds only deliberate acts while presence and chatter stay amnesiac, so the substrate cannot become a behavioral surveillance corpus. On ratification the design note refusals list gains this entry by ordinary commit. Rationale: a score silently becoming authority is the failure mode; authority changes must remain audited acts (operator direction, 2026-08-07, Promise Theory discussion)."}